WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.878
The experiments confirm every prediction.

00:00:02.958 --> 00:00:04.970
As the number of trees grows,

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:09.226
the empirical kernel converges to the closed-form
Tree NTK,

00:00:09.306 --> 00:00:12.544
and training dynamics match kernel regression.

00:00:12.624 --> 00:00:16.512
Making trees deeper first improves then hurts accuracy,

00:00:16.592 --> 00:00:18.892
exactly the predicted degeneracy.

00:00:18.972 --> 00:00:24.158
On the ninety datasets the multi-layer perceptron
kernel wins on average,

00:00:24.238 --> 00:00:28.919
but the tree kernel is better on more than thirty
percent of them,

00:00:28.999 --> 00:00:31.444
where the tree inductive bias fits.

00:00:31.524 --> 00:00:36.710
And because its cost never grows with depth, it is
far faster to compute.
